The scratch privatization tests compared sums of single-precision GEMMs with numpy's answer in
the same precision, to a tolerance relative to each entry. On conda-forge's Linux build an entry
of 0.108 that cancels from terms of about 86 missed it, though Einsums was off by only 8e-8: the
float32 reference itself was off by 2.2e-6. Fixed in Einsums after 2.0.0a1.

